From c7cf4aae956ea0db9253b6592749c578d1546ce5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Milos Nikic <nikic.milos@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Jan 2026 22:04:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] st: scrollback reflow and selection across scrollback

Reflow the scrollback buffer on resize instead of dropping it: wrapped
lines are joined into logical lines and re-split to the new width.

Keep the selection in logical rows spanning history and screen (0 is
the oldest scrollback line, sb.len + y is screen row y) instead of in
window coordinates. Lines keep their row when pushed into scrollback,
so the selection now survives scrolling the view and new output, and
can cover more than one screen. Only evicting the oldest line from the
ring shifts it.

- shift+click extends the current selection: the end nearest to the
  click follows it, keeping word/line snapping. Disabled in MODE_MOUSE,
  where shift forces selection instead.
- scrolling the wheel while dragging keeps the selection end under the
  pointer.
- typing while scrolled back no longer clears the selection.
- the selection is cleared when the width changes (reflow) or the alt
  screen is resized, and kept on height-only resizes.
